{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44115648",
      "title": "There's More Than One Way Of Binding CSS Classes Dynamically",
      "lectureOrder": 120,
      "videoOrder": 114,
      "sourceHash": "4cb6753e112ed9c953f2bb0ea7912a836f167e2c70e2a9a331fd2bced90186ac",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.24,
          "end": 2.46,
          "en": "So how else can you bind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.46,
          "end": 4.893,
          "en": "and set classes dynamically?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.94,
          "end": 9.24,
          "en": "Well, besides using this syntax which allows you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.24,
          "end": 12.54,
          "en": "to add a single class dynamically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.54,
          "end": 15.48,
          "en": "you can also use a different syntax that allows you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.48,
          "end": 20.283,
          "en": "to dynamically control multiple classes simultaneously.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.18,
          "end": 24.4,
          "en": "For that, you have to remove this .status here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.29,
          "end": 28.953,
          "en": "and instead set class to an object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 30.51,
          "end": 35.43,
          "en": "And this object can now contain multiple key value pairs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 35.43,
          "end": 39.78,
          "en": "where every key represents one CSS class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 39.78,
          "end": 44.43,
          "en": "You wanna set dynamically and the value should yield true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 44.43,
          "end": 47.07,
          "en": "or false depending on whether that class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 47.07,
          "end": 48.753,
          "en": "should be added or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 49.83,
          "end": 51.33,
          "en": "So for example, we could say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 51.33,
          "end": 54.9,
          "en": "that the status class should always be added,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 54.9,
          "end": 57.34,
          "en": "so we could simply set this to true,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 57.34,
          "end": 61.56,
          "en": "but then as an additional key value pair,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 61.56,
          "end": 66.303,
          "en": "we might wanna conditionally add the status online class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 68.31,
          "end": 71.16,
          "en": "And for that we have to add status-online",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 71.16,
          "end": 75.33,
          "en": "as a property and then define the condition",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 75.33,
          "end": 79.11,
          "en": "that determines whether this is added or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 79.11,
          "end": 82.32,
          "en": "So in my case here, that current status must be equal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 82.32,
          "end": 85.023,
          "en": "to online for this class to be applied.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 87.09,
          "end": 88.95,
          "en": "Now if you were to save it like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 88.95,
          "end": 90.81,
          "en": "you'd get an error though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 90.81,
          "end": 95.34,
          "en": "because this is actually an invalid property name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 95.34,
          "end": 96.69,
          "en": "In JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 96.69,
          "end": 100.53,
          "en": "and TypeScript, you can't add properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 100.53,
          "end": 105.53,
          "en": "that include dashes or white space like this to an object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 105.9,
          "end": 108.96000000000001,
          "en": "Even though I'm not seeing an error here in my IDE,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 108.96000000000001,
          "end": 111.07300000000001,
          "en": "this is not something you can do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 111.07300000000001,
          "end": 116.07300000000001,
          "en": "Instead, if you have properties that must contain a dash,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 116.97,
          "end": 121.97,
          "en": "like here where my class I'm targeting has a dash.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 122.64,
          "end": 126,
          "en": "In such situations, you have to convert these properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 126,
          "end": 129.003,
          "en": "to strings by wrapping them with quotes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 130.05,
          "end": 133.62,
          "en": "This is allowed by both JavaScript and TypeScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 133.62,
          "end": 136.65,
          "en": "and therefore now this will be added as a class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 136.65,
          "end": 140.013,
          "en": "dynamically to this diff if this condition is met.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 142.05,
          "end": 145.11,
          "en": "And we can now also add status-offline",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 145.11,
          "end": 149.53,
          "en": "if current status is equal to offline",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 150.84,
          "end": 155.84,
          "en": "or add status dash unknown as a class to the diff",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 156.32999999999998,
          "end": 159.633,
          "en": "if current status is equal to unknown.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 163.26,
          "end": 166.2,
          "en": "Well and with that, if you save that, the error goes away.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 166.2,
          "end": 168.66,
          "en": "And this now looks differently",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 168.66,
          "end": 173.07999999999998,
          "en": "because now we got this blinking purple text here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 173.97,
          "end": 175.697,
          "en": "and we have that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 175.697,
          "end": 178.82999999999998,
          "en": "because we're now adding those classes dynamically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 178.82999999999998,
          "end": 180.53,
          "en": "Though of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 180.53,
          "end": 181.77,
          "en": "at the moment it's not too dynamic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 181.77,
          "end": 184.38,
          "en": "because this is hard coded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 184.38,
          "end": 186.99,
          "en": "Of course, I can change it here, and if I do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 186.99,
          "end": 190.01,
          "en": "and I save that, I see the different styles in action,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 190.01,
          "end": 193.71,
          "en": "but it never changes once the application is running.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 193.71,
          "end": 195.663,
          "en": "But we'll take care of that soon.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
